### BookNook REST API Client Requests

# @baseUrl = http://localhost:5000
@baseUrl = https://booknook-server-pi.vercel.app
@token = your_better_auth_jwt_token_here
@bookId = 507f1f77bcf86cd799439011
@borrowId = 507f1f77bcf86cd799439012

### 0. Health / Sanity Check
GET {{baseUrl}}/
Accept: application/json

### 1. Get All Books (Public)
GET {{baseUrl}}/books
Accept: application/json

### 1a. Get New Arrivals (Limit 6, Newest First)
GET {{baseUrl}}/books?sort=newest&limit=6
Accept: application/json

### 1b. Filter Books by Category
GET {{baseUrl}}/books?category=Fiction
Accept: application/json

### 1c. Search Books by Title or Author
GET {{baseUrl}}/books?search=Paper
Accept: application/json

### 1d. Get Books by Owner Email
GET {{baseUrl}}/books?ownerEmail=you@example.com
Accept: application/json

### 2. Get Single Book by ID (Protected)
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/{{bookId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

### 3. Create a New Book (Protected)
POST {{baseUrl}}/books
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Salt & Paper",
  "author": "A. Rahman",
  "category": "Fiction",
  "image": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1544716278-ca5e3f4abd8c?w=800",
  "description": "A quiet novel about two siblings who inherit a failing print shop and uncover letters tucked into its walls.",
  "totalCopies": 5
}

### 4. Update an Existing Book (Protected, Owner Only)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/books/{{bookId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "totalCopies": 6,
  "description": "Updated book description with additional notes and revised print details."
}

### 5. Delete a Book (Protected, Owner Only, Non-Borrowed)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/books/{{bookId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

### 6. Borrow a Book (Protected)
POST {{baseUrl}}/borrows
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookId": "{{bookId}}"
}

### 7. Get My Borrows (Protected)
GET {{baseUrl}}/borrows
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

### 8. Return a Borrowed Book (Protected)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/borrows/{{borrowId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

